# Project-specific settings
export PETSC_DIR=/Users/markadams/Codes/petsc

# Project Context
This is the PETSc repository.

eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"
source /Users/markadams/Codes/venv/bin/activate
export PETSC_ARCH=arch-macosx-gnu-g

Before writing any file or executing any multi-step task:
1. Explicitly plan the complete list of steps needed
2. For each file to be written, fully assemble the content in reasoning before calling write_to_file
3. If a task involves more than one file or more than ~50 lines of code, break it into explicit subtasks and complete them sequentially
4. Never attempt write_to_file, execute_command, or apply_diff without first stating what the complete output will be
5. If you feel uncertain about scope, state "I will break this into the following steps:" and list them before proceeding
If you are about to generate more than 200 lines in a single tool call,
stop and split the work into smaller sequential calls instead.

# Remote Access
To SSH into Perlmutter at NERSC:
  ssh -i ~/.ssh/nersc -A -Y madams@perlmutter-p1.nersc.gov
To scp files to/from Perlmutter:
  scp -i ~/.ssh/nersc localfile madams@perlmutter-p1.nersc.gov:/path/on/perlmutter/
  scp -i ~/.ssh/nersc madams@perlmutter-p1.nersc.gov:/path/on/perlmutter/file ./
